om/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99570","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99570","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99570.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99570.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixed the calculation of inertia for polygons.\r\nBefore, the inertia of it's aabb was calculated.\r\nThis lead to incoherent behavior like in issue #55148.\r\nIn that issue, it is described how a misaligned square calculates the inertia of a larger aabb square, leading to twice the inertia, and a slower rotating square when compared to an aligned one.\r\nTo fix this I replace the inertia calculation for the formula of inertia for polygons.\r\nThe issue is fixed as can be seen in the zipped project.\r\nThe square shape, the aligned square polygon, and the misaligned square polygon, all calculate the same inertia, and rotate equally.\r\n\r\n[test-inertia.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17878209/test-inertia.zip)\r\n\r\n<i>Bugsquad edit:</i>\r\n- Fix #55148","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99570/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99570/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}